# Database migrations

Production MySQL can fail or block too long when constraint/index names are auto-generated (long names) or when heavy DDL is bundled in one migration.

## Required: short custom names

Always set explicit **short** names for:

- Foreign keys → `{abbr}_{ref}_fk` (e.g. `pa_user_fk`)
- Indexes → `{abbr}_{purpose}_idx` (e.g. `pa_paid_at_idx`)
- Unique → `{abbr}_{purpose}_uq`

Target **under 48 characters** (MySQL limit 64). Use table abbreviations from `database/MIGRATION_CONVENTIONS.md`.

## Foreign keys

Do **not** rely on default `foreignId()->constrained()` names on new migrations.

```php
// ✅ GOOD
$table->foreignId('user_id')->nullable();
$table->foreign('user_id', MigrationNames::fk('pa', 'user'))
    ->references('id')->on('users')
    ->nullOnDelete();

// down():
$table->dropForeign(MigrationNames::fk('pa', 'user'));
$table->dropColumn('user_id');
```

```php
// ❌ BAD (auto name, often too long)
$table->foreignId('user_id')->nullable()->constrained('users')->nullOnDelete();
$table->dropForeign(['user_id']);
```

## Indexes

```php
$table->index(['paid_at', 'project_id'], MigrationNames::idx('pa', 'paid_proj'));
$table->dropIndex(MigrationNames::idx('pa', 'paid_proj'));
```

## Production-safe DDL

- One heavy change per migration when altering large tables (add column → backfill → FK/index in follow-up if needed).
- Prefer nullable column first, then enforce FK after data exists.
- Do not add multiple FKs + indexes on `project_allocations`, `projects`, `manhours` in a single migration unless trivial.
- In `down()`, drop by **custom name** (same string as `up()`).

## Reference

See `database/MIGRATION_CONVENTIONS.md` and `App\Support\MigrationNames`.
